<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Renault workers vote to resume work-radio.</title>
<headline>Belgian Renault workers vote to resume work-radio.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A majority of workers at the Belgian Vilvoorde assembly plant of French car maker Renault SA on Thursday voted to resume work, Belgian radio said.</p>
<p>BRTN radio said 2,721 of the Vilvoorde plant's 3,100 employees voted in Thursday's referendum on a possible continuation of a five-week stoppage started after Renault headquarters decided to close the profitable plant by the end of July.</p>
<p>It said 68.7 percent of the workers voted for a resumption of work. Production would now resume on Monday, it added.</p>
</text>
